    },
    "A DuckDB database reads these when it opens. To change one that is open, run SET memory_limit = '4GB' or SET threads = 4 in a card. Each open database has its own limit, so several open databases can use more in all." : {

    },
    "A Partitions folder under each partitioned table." : {

    },
    "A Session can keep %@ of results. The queries were saved; run them again after you open the Session." : {

    },
    "A Session named '%@' already exists in this folder." : {

    },
    "A TSV export always uses a tab, whatever this says." : {

    },
    "A banner shows while a tab has a transaction open. 0 turns the timeout off; a forgotten transaction then holds its locks until you commit, roll back or close the tab." : {

    },
    "A card failed or was cancelled, so DuckDB aborted the transaction. Its changes cannot be committed. Roll back to run more cards." : {

    },
    "A card you have named is never touched. Tabs take the name of their connection and schema." : {

    },
    "A ceiling on the whole history, newest kept. 0 is no ceiling. Both limits apply: whichever removes an entry first wins." : {

    },
    "A connection that names none keeps every schema by name." : {

    },
    "A copy also carries the TSV form, so a paste into a spreadsheet lands as a table whichever this says." : {

    },
    "A faint wash behind the line holding the caret." : {

    },
    "A glyph for the data type beside its name in the column header." : {

    },
    "A larger batch is fewer round trips and more memory at once. 5000 is what every export used before this was a setting." : {

    },
    "A list that is all numbers, all booleans or all NULL is left bare whichever this says — quoting it would change what it means." : {

    },
    "A log scale needs every value above zero." : {

    },
    "A password you type into a connection that does not remember it is held until Pharos quits." : {

    },
    "A paste that looks like bare values offers a “Format as SQL list” button." : {

    },
    "A pool is built when a connection opens, so these numbers reach a connection the next time you connect it — never a connection that is already open." : {

    },
    "A query that fails leaves a row in the history, with the server's message, beside the ones that worked." : {

    },
    "A query that finishes in a tab you are not viewing." : {

    },
    "A result on disk stays on its card and opens again at once; macOS reads it back as you scroll. 0 keeps every result in memory." : {

    },
    "A row the action means nothing for — a schema, a column — still expands. Describe opens the table's DDL sheet, and only a plain table has one." : {

    },
    "A row with more tags is not hiding them: the tooltip and the Inspector always list every one." : {

    },
    "A sentence above an EXPLAIN result saying what the planner chose." : {

    },
    "A shorter region gets no chevron." : {

    },
    "A small server allows few connections. Over the limit, a tab's cards run on the shared pool, without session state between cards. 0 = no limit. A DuckDB database has no limit: each tab always has its own connection." : {

    },
    "A tab that has never been saved is only mentioned while Restore open tabs is off." : {

    },
    "A tag marks the rows whose values match its rules — an address, a CIDR range, a number, a date." : {
      "comment" : "Tag Manager: the empty state's message."
    },
    "A variable is a named value that a query uses as {{name}} — text, a number, a date, a list." : {
      "comment" : "Variable Manager: the empty state's message."
